.TH GENFONT 8
.SH NAME
genfont \- regenerate the console font
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 tools/genfont.py
.RB [ \-\-preview ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Genfont
rasterises a monospace TrueType font on the host into the one bitmap
font table Vectra has, and writes it to standard output as Odin
source:
.IP
.EX
python3 tools/genfont.py > sys/libfont/font_data.odin
.EE
.PP
.B sys/libfont
is imported by the kernel's console and linked by any ring 3 program
that draws text, so there is one table and nothing to keep in step
between them.
Nothing is rasterised at boot.
.PP
The source font is
.BR PTMono.ttc ,
read from the host's own font directory, rasterised at 13 pixels into
an 8 by 16 cell: twelve rows above the baseline and four below, which
is exactly what that face gives at that size.
Ninety-five glyphs are baked, the printable ASCII range from
.B 0x20
to
.BR 0x7E .
Each cell is one bit per pixel, one byte per scanline, most
significant bit leftmost, and a pixel is lit when the rasteriser's
coverage there passes a fixed threshold.
.PP
.B \-\-preview
renders a handful of glyphs as text art on standard output instead of
writing the table, for a quick look at the shapes without touching the
generated file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
just font
python3 tools/genfont.py --preview
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B sys/libfont/font_data.odin
generated.
Not edited by hand.
.SH SOURCE
.B tools/genfont.py
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR build (8),
.IR font (2)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Requires Python 3 with Pillow.
Nothing else in the tree needs either.
